        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You came to the forest for something simple.</strong><br><strong>To breathe. To walk. To fish, hunt, gather mushrooms — and disappear from the noise for a while.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then something found you first. You wake up alone in the middle of the woods, disoriented. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Somewhere in the distance, you spot an old fire lookout tower. It’s the only landmark you have. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Maybe the only chance you have left.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/4092b35c7bbaf10273c7774c7e9fe219.poster.avif?t=1788363065\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/4092b35c7bbaf10273c7774c7e9fe219.webm?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/4092b35c7bbaf10273c7774c7e9fe219.mp4?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Forest That Feels Real</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Forest Doesn’t Care throws you into a dense, living wilderness inspired by real terrain:<br>deep forests, swamps, hills, abandoned places, hidden paths, and long stretches of silence that feel almost too real.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Survive, Explore, and Follow the Trail</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What begins as a desperate search for help slowly turns into something much stranger.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Reach remote towers.<br>Search abandoned places.<br>Follow traces left by people who came before you.<br>Meet the few who still live here — and decide whether they are helping you, using you, or lying to you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/c97c27681efef7748e01404c3c0b95f9.poster.avif?t=1788363065\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/c97c27681efef7748e01404c3c0b95f9.webm?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/c97c27681efef7748e01404c3c0b95f9.mp4?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Grounded Survival</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is not a base-building sandbox.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You won’t be cutting down forests or constructing massive structures.  Survival here is practical, limited, and grounded in reality. You are not here to conquer the forest. <br>You are here to survive it.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Play Your Way</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Whether you want a quiet life in the woods or a brutal fight to survive, the game offers multiple ways to play:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Peaceful</strong> — explore, fish, gather, and enjoy the forest at your own pace</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Survival</strong> — balance freedom, danger, and the need to stay alive</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hardcore</strong> — harsher conditions, higher risk, less forgiveness</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One Life</strong> — no second chances</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What starts as a search for help can turn into a calm life in the wilderness…<br>or your worst mistake.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/8849b5e6b9e797585cd5a5eaef4badd1.poster.avif?t=1788363065\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/8849b5e6b9e797585cd5a5eaef4badd1.webm?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/8849b5e6b9e797585cd5a5eaef4badd1.mp4?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Not Quite Horror. Something Worse.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is not a traditional horror game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no cheap haunted house tricks here.<br>But the deeper you go, the more the forest begins to feel wrong.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Strange symbols.<br>Unfinished messages.<br>Improvised rituals.<br>People who speak like they know more than they should.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And signs that something in this place has been waiting much longer than you’ve been alive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/8415a7b7eb95aaafb2b6950c40690a6b.poster.avif?t=1788363065\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/8415a7b7eb95aaafb2b6950c40690a6b.webm?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3922100/extras/8415a7b7eb95aaafb2b6950c40690a6b.mp4?t=1788363065\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Play Alone or With Others</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the forest solo or with friends in multiplayer.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Travel together, survive together, argue over supplies, get lost, or sit by the fire —<br>before everything goes wrong again.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The forest doesn’t care how many of you there are.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>NVIDIA DLSS &amp; Reflex Support</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Experience the forest the way it was meant to be seen.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Forest Doesn’t Care pushes dense, lifelike environments to the limit — with tens of thousands of trees, dynamic lighting, and rich atmospheric detail.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With NVIDIA DLSS, you can boost performance using AI-powered upscaling without sacrificing visual quality.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For players seeking the absolute best image, <strong>DLAA</strong> (Deep Learning Anti-Aliasing) delivers maximum clarity and detail — perfect for capturing every branch, shadow, and movement in the forest.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And with NVIDIA Reflex, gameplay becomes more responsive, reducing system latency and ensuring every movement feels precise and immediate.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choose your balance between performance and visual fidelity — and step into a forest that feels truly alive.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i>## Developer’s Note</i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Forest Doesn't Care was created by a two-person team driven by one goal: to build a forest that doesn't feel like a level, but like a real place. A place where you can fish, hunt, camp, survive, get lost — and gradually realize that something is deeply wrong here. Everything in this project grew far beyond what we originally planned — the world, the systems, the secrets, the danger, and the freedom we wanted to give the player. </i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>We are incredibly grateful to everyone who has been with us since the early days — back when this was just a quiet mushroom-picking experience. </i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Somewhere along the way, the project took on a life of its own.</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>And we decided to follow it as far as it goes.</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
